    "created_at": "2021-04-08T23:46:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-04-08T23:46:08Z",
    "body": "What should be displayed for these modules? On my personal systems, I typically have both gcc and clang installed. On some work systems, it's a nice day if I only have 3 C/C++ compiler suites installed. Do I display the version of gcc? version of clang?\r\n\r\nIntuitively, I'd like for the module to display the compiler that would be used to build the code in the current directory, but what if it's an xmake project? Do we have to parse the xmake file to figure out what compiler will be used? What if that depends on an environmental variable? (e.g. `if (env(PROJECT_USE_CLANG)) CXX = clang++ else CXX = g++` in the config file).\r\n\r\nI think there are answers to these questions, but we probably want to avoid being potentially misleading (e.g. preferentially selecting `gcc` will yield the wrong result on BSD systems, where clang is the default compiler). My first thought is to allow the user to specify a list of compilers that will be searched in order (e.g. `[gcc, clang, pgcc, icc, cc]`), but I don't know how to make that correctly interact with build systems.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
